## Coding Constraints & Guidelines

### TypeScript Rules

- **No Enums**: Do not use the `enum` keyword (`erasableSyntaxOnly` constraint). Define configuration and constants as `as const` objects instead.
- **Explicit Type Imports**: Use `import type` when importing types/interfaces only (enforced by `verbatimModuleSyntax`).
- **No Unused Code**: Clean up unused imports, variables, and arguments (`noUnusedLocals` and `noUnusedParameters` are strict).

### Centralized Constants

- Never add magic numbers or strings directly to logic files.
- **Extension Backend**: Place backend-specific values in [src/constants.ts](file:///Users/monaliza/Documents/ml-projects/pixel-agents/adapters/vscode/constants.ts).
- **Webview UI**: Place frontend numbers, strings, physics, and canvas rules in [webview-ui/src/constants.ts](file:///Users/monaliza/Documents/ml-projects/pixel-agents/webview-ui/src/constants.ts).
- **Webview Styling**: Define variables and themes in the `:root` block of [index.css](file:///Users/monaliza/Documents/ml-projects/pixel-agents/webview-ui/src/index.css) using `--pixel-*` custom properties.

### Canvas Game Loop Rules

- **Imperative rendering**: Do not use React state to drive the game loop or updates on [OfficeCanvas.tsx](file:///Users/monaliza/Documents/ml-projects/pixel-agents/webview-ui/src/office/components/OfficeCanvas.tsx). Store positions, frames, layouts, pathfinding maps, and velocities in the imperative `OfficeState` class instance.
- **Pixel-Perfect Zoom**: The camera zoom must always be an integer device-pixels-per-sprite-pixel value (between `1x` and `10x`). Avoid standard canvas scaling.
- **Z-Sorting**: Z-sort entities by their Y coordinate at render-time. 
  - Standard furniture/characters use `ch.y + TILE_SIZE/2 + 0.5`.
  - Chairs: Non-back chairs use `zY = (row+1)*TILE_SIZE` (render in front), back-facing chairs use `zY = (row+1)*TILE_SIZE + 1` (chair back renders in front of characters).
  - Surface items use `zY = max(spriteBottom, deskZY + 0.5)` to overlay on desks.

### File I/O & Persistence

- **Atomic Writes**: When writing user layout/config files, write to a `.tmp` file and rename it atomically (`fs.promises.rename`) to prevent corruption.
- **Path Sanitization**: Ensure workspace paths are sanitized, removing colons, backslashes, and forward slashes.

### Session & Status Tracking

- **Dual-Mode Tracking**: System defaults to **Hooks mode** (Fastify server receiving events from Claude Code hooks via `~/.pixel-agents/hooks/claude-hook.js`). If hooks are not installed or active, falls back to **Heuristic mode** (polling log transcripts).
- **Polling Watcher**: Maintain the single-polling approach (500ms intervals) for JSONL file changes. Use partial line buffering to safely carry incomplete or unterminated line reads.
- **Delaying Tool Completion**: Add a `300ms` delay on `agentToolDone` events to prevent rendering flicker caused by React batching.
- **Idle Detection**: Turn completion uses either the turn duration event from transcripts (98% of cases) or fallback text-idle timer (`TEXT_IDLE_DELAY_MS = 5000`) for text-only interactions.
